      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Read\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [26, 19, 28]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 14.44 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nAn analysis of the accessibility of the read/write operations mentioned in the defect report is as follows.\n\n### Accessibility Analysis of Operations\n\n1.  **Write to `g` at line 26 in `svp_simple_636_001_main()`**\n    - **Operation:** `g = 1;`\n    - **Control Conditions:** This operation is not guarded by any control statements.\n    - **Execution Analysis:** This line is part of the main execution flow of the `svp_simple_636_001_main` function. It is executed unconditionally after the program starts.\n    - **Conclusion:** The operation is **executable**.\n\n2.  **Read from `g` at line 19 in `svp_simple_636_001_isr_1()`**\n    - **Operation:** `if (g == 1)`\n    - **Control Conditions:** This read operation is part of the condition `if (g == 1)`. The operation is executed if the interrupt handler `svp_simple_636_001_isr_1` is triggered.\n    - **Execution Analysis:** The system model allows an interrupt to preempt the main task. A possible execution scenario is:\n        1. The `main` function executes `g = 1;` at line 26.\n        2. Before the `main` function executes `g = 2;` at line 28, an interrupt occurs, and `svp_simple_636_001_isr_1` starts executing.\n        3. Inside the ISR, the condition `if (g == 1)` at line 19 is evaluated. At this point, the value of `g` is `1`. The read of `g` occurs, and the condition evaluates to true.\n    - **Conclusion:** The operation is **executable**.\n\n3.  **Write to `g` at line 28 in `svp_simple_636_001_main()`**\n    - **Operation:** `g = 2;`\n    - **Control Conditions:** This operation is not guarded by any control statements.\n    - **Execution Analysis:** This line is part of the main execution flow. It will be executed after the operation at line 26, potentially after being preempted by the ISR.\n    - **Conclusion:** The operation is **executable**.\n\n### Final Conclusion\n\nAll read/write operations listed in the defect report are executable. The reported atomicity violation describes a valid scenario:\n1.  **Write:** `main` executes `g = 1;` (line 26).\n2.  **Preemption:** `svp_simple_636_001_isr_1` preempts `main`.\n3.  **Read:** The ISR reads `g` in the condition `if (g == 1)` (line 19), observing the intermediate value `1`.\n4.  **Resume:** `main` resumes and executes the second part of its update.\n5.  **Write:** `main` executes `g = 2;` (line 28).\n\nThis sequence constitutes a valid Write-Read-Write atomicity violation. The original report is correct.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Read\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"26\", \"19\", \"28\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
